### 3.3 What the verification proves

| Check | Evidence |
|---|---|
| Exact predicates agree with a high‑precision reference | `orient2d`: 100 000/100 000 exact matches (70 184 raw‑float sign errors, 100 000 filter fallbacks). `orient3d`: 100 000/100 000 exact matches (319 raw‑float sign errors, 815 fallbacks). `incircle`/`insphere`: 50 000/50 000 matches against a BigInt determinant. |
| `V − E + F == 2` | Asserted on every 3D facet set and on the doubled 2D polygon (`V−E+F = n−n+2`). |
| Consistent winding / manifold | Each undirected facet edge has one positive and one negative directed occurrence. |
| Non‑degenerate facets | Exact collinearity test on the first three vertices of every facet, plus strict convexity of every facet polygon. |
| No point strictly outside | Exact half‑space test over all input points vs every facet. |
| Normal away from interior | Exact dyadic `orient3d(facet, interior) < 0`, interior = exact dyadic centroid of the initial simplex. |
| Coplanar degeneracy | All‑coplanar inputs degrade to a 2D polygon; convex, containing all points, with two opposite facets. |
| Coplanar points on a facet plane | The box‑with‑lattice‑faces test yields exactly 8 vertices and 6 facets; brute‑force boundary coverage of 399 random sets shows no missed supporting plane. |
| Duplicates / cospherical ties | Permuted‑duplicate and sphere/grid tests pass all invariants. |
| Scale | 2000 cospherical points build + fully verify in ≈1.4 s. |
